  `CDbCriteria::__construct`  public constructor, callable with zero arguments
  public instance properties  `select`, `distinct`, `condition`, `params`,
                              `limit`, `offset`, `order`, `group`, `having` —
                              each publicly readable and writable on a live
                              instance
  `CDbCriteria::__wakeup()`   public magic method, zero parameters; reached both
                              via `unserialize()` and via direct invocation on a
                              live instance
  Instances must pass through PHP `serialize()` / `unserialize()`; both
  round-trip entry points are driven by the retained callers.

## Called as
  Construction and property writes — callers create an instance and write public
  properties before any serialization step:

      $criteria = new CDbCriteria();
      $criteria->condition = ...;   // a string
      $criteria->params    = ...;   // an array with string keys; values are
                                    // strings or integers
      $criteria->params["..."] = ...;   // single-entry write, same shapes
      $criteria->select    = ...;   // an array of strings
      $criteria->order     = ...;   // a string
      $criteria->group     = ...;   // a string
      $criteria->having    = ...;   // a string
      $criteria->limit     = ...;   // an integer
      $criteria->offset    = ...;   // an integer
      $criteria->distinct  = ...;   // a boolean

  `params`, like every property listed above, is a plain public property with no
  declared type: any value of any type is syntactically assignable to it.

  Counter positioning — callers assign the static counter before serialization
  and again before the restoring step:

      CDbCriteria::$paramCount = ...;   // an integer

  Round-trip entry point — PHP calls `__wakeup()` itself during `unserialize()`:

      $serialized = serialize($criteria);
      $restored   = unserialize($serialized);

  `unserialize()` receives one input: a string. Callers pass strings; no
  guarantee about the content of that string accompanies the call.

  Direct magic-method entry point:

      $criteria->__wakeup();

  Zero arguments, invoked on a live `CDbCriteria` instance whose public
  properties (including `condition`, `params`, and `CDbCriteria::$paramCount`)
  were written beforehand.

