  Module-level function in `sabnzbd/newsunpack.py`; imported by name into `sabnzbd/notifier.py`. Retained callers `external_processing` and `pre_queue` in this file pass the job plus an extra-fields mapping and hand the result to the subprocess launcher as the process environment; the notifier'"'"'s script runner calls it with no arguments.
- **Observable behavior:** Builds the environment mapping delivered to user scripts: a copy of the daemon'"'"'s own environment extended with `SAB_<NAME>` entries, where `<NAME>` is a field name uppercased. One entry per field of the retained `ENV_NZO_FIELDS` list read from the job when one is given; one entry per caller-supplied extra field; and always the program facts under the field names `program_dir`, `par2_command`, `multipar_command`, `rar_command`, `zip_command`, `7zip_command`, `version`.
- **Inputs:** Optional `NzbObject` job; optional mapping of extra field names to values.
