```
- **Required interface:** Trait attribute `pod_name_template`, declared at class scope on `KubeSpawner` as a `traitlets.Unicode` trait with `config=True`. It is reached by `KubeSpawner.__init__`, which reads it as `self.pod_name_template` and passes it to the single-template expansion method (`self._expand_user_properties(self.pod_name_template)`) to produce `self.pod_name`. It is also externally configurable by JupyterHub configuration as `c.KubeSpawner.pod_name_template`. The default value is the literal string the trait initializes to when no config overrides it; it begins with `jupyter-` and substitutes the escaped user name and the escaped server name. The `config=True` visibility is required so JupyterHub config can set it.
- **Observable behavior:** Provides the template string from which `pod_name` is derived during construction. Its `{username}` and `{servername}` placeholders are substituted with the escaped, DNS-label-safe forms of the user name and server name. The default template causes the produced `pod_name` to begin with the literal prefix `jupyter-`.
- **Inputs:** None at call time; it is a declarative trait with a default. The substitution inputs (`self.user.name`, `self.user.id`, `self.name`) are consumed by the expansion method, not by this declaration.
- **Outputs and errors:** A `Unicode` trait instance assigned to the class attribute `pod_name_template`; its default is a template that begins with `jupyter-` and substitutes the escaped user name and the escaped server name. No errors.
