### proxy.html
Masked section 1:
```
- **Required interface:** The document itself is the interface, consumed by two routes:
  - `GET /proxy.html` on the app origin — the file lives at `/app/proxy.html` and is served at that path by the static file server on port 8080. Pages on other origins fetch it and embed it in an iframe; the library'"'"'s `sysend.proxy` default addressing appends exactly this path segment to a URL that does not end in `.html`, so the name and `.html` extension are consumed.
  - A relative script include, the document'"'"'s load-bearing content: `<script src="sysend.js"></script>`. Relative resolution is what makes the relay endpoint work: when the document is fetched at `<origin>/proxy.html`, the script resolves to `<origin>/sysend.js`, so the instance inside the iframe always runs the app-origin copy of the library regardless of which origin embedded the document. The script loads synchronously during document parsing (no deferred or asynchronous loading).
- **Observable behavior:** A minimal HTML page whose single functional role is to load the sysend.js library in this document'"'"'s own origin (the app origin) so that, when embedded as an iframe by a page on another origin, an initialized library instance runs here and acts as the endpoint that carries events between the two origins. The document carries no interactive content; the endpoint behavior itself is provided by the library it loads.
- **Inputs:** The HTTP request that fetches the document, and — when embedded — the relay frames the embedding page posts to the iframe'"'"'s window. The library instance receives and acts on those frames.
- **Outputs and errors:** The served document; after its load event, an initialized library instance exists in the document'"'"'s own origin. In the normal mode of consumption — embedded in an iframe on another origin — the instance detects the embedded context, registers the relay listener that receives window message frames addressed to the iframe'"'"'s window and re-broadcasts the frames it accepts as events on this origin'"'"'s channel, and joins this origin'"'"'s channel like any other window. All of this behavior is the library'"'"'s contract (specified with `sysend.js`); this document'"'"'s contract is centred on loading that file at this origin.
- **Side effects and interactions:** Single dependency: the sibling file `sysend.js` in the same directory, resolved by the relative script tag. No other imports, assets, styles, or packages; no build step. The document imposes no state of its own: reloading it or embedding it again produces a fresh library instance with the same behavior, and nothing about it persists between loads.
- **Required sequencing and state:** The script executes during document parsing, and by the document'"'"'s load event the library instance is initialized — in embedded mode, with its relay listener registered. Callers interact with the frame only after it has loaded. Whether the instance behaves as embedded or top-level is decided by the library, not by this document.
- **Region boundary:** Self-contained. The region is the entire file, from the doctype through the closing `html` element, with nothing retained above or below it; the replacement must be a complete, well-formed HTML document. The doctype, the charset declaration, the advisory robots meta tag, element whitespace, and the surrounding markup scaffolding are unconsumed detail and may differ; the fixed surface is the path, the relative script include, and the resulting loaded embedded instance.
